  "title": "List of largest banks",
  "pageid": 38298344,
  "revid": 1375587500,
  "text": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><p>The following are lists of the largest <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Commercial_banks\" title=\"Commercial banks\">commercial banks</a> in the world, as measured by total <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Assets\" title=\"Assets\">assets</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Market_capitalization\" title=\"Market capitalization\">market capitalization</a>.\n</p><p>This list is based on the April 2026 <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/S%26P_Global_Market_Intelligence\" title=\"S&amp;P Global Market Intelligence\">S&amp;P Global Market Intelligence</a> report of the 100 largest banks in the world. The ranking was based upon assets as reported and was not adjusted for different accounting treatments.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-SP_1-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SP-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Another publication which compiles an annual list of the world's largest banks is <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Banker\" title=\"The Banker\">The Banker</a></i> magazine. It publishes a list of the World 1000 Largest Banks every July.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The financial data published by the July yearly issue of <i>The Banker</i> are much more extensive compared to the S&amp;P Top 100 banks, but it is not a publication intended for the general public.\n</p><p>Accounting treatment affects the assets reported: for example, the United States uses <a href=\"/wiki/Generally_Accepted_Accounting_Principles_(United_States)\" title=\"Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (United States)\">US GAAP</a> (as opposed to <a href=\"/wiki/International_Financial_Reporting_Standards\" title=\"International Financial Reporting Standards\">IFRS</a>), which only reports the net <a href=\"/wiki/Derivative_(finance)\" title=\"Derivative (finance)\">derivative</a> position in most cases, leading to US banks having fewer derivative assets than comparable non-US banks.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> When adjusted forward this netting, JPMorgan Chase would have <span>US$4,607.43</span><span class=\"nowrap\"> </span>billion in total assets, rather than <span>US$4,002.81</span><span class=\"nowrap\"> </span>billion.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-SP_1-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SP-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> However, this has no impact on the ranking of the bank.\n</p><table class=\"wikitable sortable mw-collapsible\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th data-sort-type=\"number\">Rank\n</th>\n<th>Bank name\n</th>\n<th>Total assets<br/>(April 2026)<br/>(<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/US$\" title=\"US$\">US$</a> billion)\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/China\" title=\"China\"><img alt=\"China\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"15\" width=\"23\"/></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Industrial_and_Commercial_Bank_of_China\" title=\"Industrial and Commercial Bank of China\">Industrial and Commercial Bank of China</a>\n</td>\n<td>7,645.80\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/China\" title=\"China\"><img alt=\"China\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"15\" width=\"23\"/></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Agricultural_Bank_of_China\" title=\"Agricultural Bank of China\">Agricultural Bank of China</a>\n</td>\n<td>6,974.82\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/China\" title=\"China\"><img alt=\"China\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"15\" width=\"23\"/></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/China_Construction_Bank\" title=\"China Construction Bank\">China Construction Bank</a>\n</td>\n<td>6,524.05\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/China\" title=\"China\"><img alt=\"China\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"15\" width=\"23\"/></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Bank_of_China\" title=\"Bank of China\">Bank of China</a>\n</td>\n<td>5,484.11\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/United_States\" title=\"United States\"><img alt=\"United States\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"12\" width=\"23\"/></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/JPMorgan_Chase\" title=\"JPMorgan Chase\">JPMorgan Chase</a>\n</td>\n<td>4,424.90\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/United_Kingdom\" title=\"United Kingdom\"><img alt=\"United Kingdom\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"12\" width=\"23\"/></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/HSBC\" title=\"HSBC\">HSBC</a>\n</td>\n<td>3,438.16\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>7\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/United_States\" title=\"United States\"><img alt=\"United States\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"12\" width=\"23\"/></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Bank_of_America\" title=\"Bank of America\">Bank of America</a>\n</td>\n<td>3,411.74\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/France\" title=\"France\"><img alt=\"France\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"15\" width=\"23\"/></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/BNP_Paribas\" title=\"BNP Paribas\">BNP Paribas</a>\n</td>\n<td>3,279.30\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeo